WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.567
-Ice, welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:03.734
And thank you for coming on.

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:05.100
We love it when you come by,
bud.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.033
-You know, it's always a treat
when players meet, man.

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:08.434
It's always a treat
-Ah, I love it.

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:10.934
[ Laughter ]
I've got to just say,

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:12.868
I'm fanboying out a little bit
here for you,

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:15.133
'cause I saw you at the Grammys,
on the --

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:19.167
This is the 50 --
50th anniversary of hip hop.

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:20.834
The tribute to hip hop.

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:23.334
And you came out and crushed it,
buddy.

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:25.133
You were unbelievable.

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:27.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:27.234 --> 00:00:30.000
-It was all thanks to Questlove.
-It's all thanks to Questlove.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.968
-All thanks to Questlove.
I was minding my business,

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:33.133
I get a phone call.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:37.367
I mind my business.
I got a phone call.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:40.334
Quest says, "Man, I need you
at the Grammys on Sunday."

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:42.634
I'm like, "I can't do it."

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:46.300
Because I'm --
We film every weekday.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.167
So, Mondays, I work.
So, I can't go

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:50.100
to the Super Bowl,
I can't go to Grammys.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.133
And he was like,
"Ice, this is gonna be epic.

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:54.434
This is not something
you want to miss."

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:56.701
And for a quick second, I said,
"I don't want to be the guy

00:00:56.701 --> 00:00:59.200
sitting at home watching it
and saying,

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.534
'You know,
they asked me to do this,'

00:01:01.534 --> 00:01:03.567
and everybody saying,
'You lying,'" you know?

00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:04.934
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:04.934 --> 00:01:07.400
-And then I also knew
Quest probably had Ice Cube

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.801
on speed dial, right?
So --

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:10.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.300
Soon as I --
So I was like, "Man, yeah."

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.901
So, I called "Law &amp; Order,"
and they said,

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:15.701
"Well, you know,
you have that episode off."

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:18.000
We take two episodes off
every season,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.334
and it was just a natural.

00:01:19.334 --> 00:01:21.701
And I went out there,
and it was with all my peers.

00:01:21.701 --> 00:01:25.567
And it was really one of
the greatest moments on stage.

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:28.267
It was only eight bars,
but it was eight bars

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:31.100
to probably the most people
I've ever performed to live

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.334
in my life.

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:35.067
-Yeah, you nailed it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:37.200
It was flawless.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.467
-Were you nervous at all?

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:40.267
-Yes.
Yeah, I was nervous.

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:42.200
Because, you know,
they running a track.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.868
And the track is coming in,
and you gotta catch your cue.

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:47.067
And, you know,
Black Thought'll tell you,

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:49.467
"You miss that cue,
the show keeps going."

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:52.334
So, I'm waiting,
and Scarface is rapping, right?

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:54.801
And there's this intro
to "New Jack Hustler" --

00:01:54.801 --> 00:01:56.667
[ Beatboxing ]

00:01:56.667 --> 00:01:59.234
But with everything going on,
everybody's having fun,

00:01:59.234 --> 00:02:01.334
but I'm listening.
You never --

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:03.033
I was listening so hard.

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:05.567
And when I heard that, I just
had to come in, "Hustler!"

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:08.467
And I was like, "I'm on beat!"
-Yeah!

00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:10.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:13.334
-But if you missed that cue,
it was a wrap,

00:02:13.334 --> 00:02:16.200
and it was gonna be very,
very, very disrespectful.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.133
It was gonna look real bad.
-You crushed it.

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:19.834
Couldn't have been
more flawless.

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:21.334
Congratulations on that.
-Thank you.

00:02:21.334 --> 00:02:23.100
-And I was, like, so happy and
so psyched to see you do that.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.100
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:29.033
-Then, right on the heels
of performing at the Grammys,

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:32.100
you got your star on
the Hollywood Walk of Fame.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.434
Look at this.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:37.167
♪♪

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:39.234
-How 'bout that?
-I got a couple photos here.

00:02:39.234 --> 00:02:41.400
Here's you with
your beautiful wife, Coco,

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.300
and your beautiful daughter,
Chanel.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:47.734
What --
What does it feel like?

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.667
Was it -- talk to me.
What is it like?

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:51.000
-Hey, man, as many times
as I got arrested

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.434
on Hollywood Boulevard
and saw those stars like this...

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:59.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:02.400
-That's the only way you saw
the stars up close, huh?

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.234
-I was like, really --
But you know what?

00:03:04.234 --> 00:03:06.434
My friends were more excited
about it than me.

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:08.734
You know, they --
It started to weigh on me

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:10.667
as it came --
got closer and closer.

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:12.400
They said,
"No, do this for your kids.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.601
Do this for everybody
that loves you."

00:03:14.601 --> 00:03:17.267
Then when I -- I went there,
South Central showed up.

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:19.667
They said, "You brought a star
back to the hood, Ice."

00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:22.100
So it became bigger and bigger.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:25.167
And then, of course, Dick Wolf
was there, Mariska was there.

00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:27.701
But it was really --
It's a star for music.

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:30.501
So, for the first time,
my "Law &amp; Order" family

00:03:30.501 --> 00:03:32.767
was surrounded
by my music family.

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:34.200
-Wow.
-So, Chuck D came,

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.033
Ice Cube came, Russell came.
It was dope.

00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:38.667
-Wow, that's so cool.

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:40.767
That's well-deserved.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:43.400
Well-deserved.
You changed the game, bud.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.934
Speaking of the game,
let's talk about your podcast,

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:48.033
"Ice-T's Daily Game," okay?

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:49.534
-Yeah.
-This is --

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:51.000
I think this is perfect for you.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.868
-Well, for the white people out
there, Black people call --

00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:56.667
Black people call
any type of wisdom "game,"

00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:59.634
'cause we figure this is the
game of life, you understand?

00:03:59.634 --> 00:04:02.767
So, when I say I'm the "daily
game," it's the game of life.

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:04.601
So, people say,
"What game are you playing?"

00:04:04.601 --> 00:04:06.634
I'm like, "I've been playing it
since I was born.

00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:08.000
This is the game of life."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.334
-This is life.
-You dig?

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:13.267
So, when I got on Twitter,
I was like, you know,

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:15.000
Twitter is mob mentality.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.801
Whoever has the most mob --
that's -- it runs Twitter.

00:04:17.801 --> 00:04:19.334
So, I said, "I gotta do
something to get people

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:21.000
to come back to my page
every day,

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.067
so I gotta do something daily."
-Yeah.

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:24.501
-And I came up with
"The Daily Game."

00:04:24.501 --> 00:04:26.834
So, it's quotes,
it's inspirational quotes.

00:04:26.834 --> 00:04:30.167
And it was going so good
on Twitter,

00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:31.734
IHeartRadio came at me and said,

00:04:31.734 --> 00:04:35.300
"Let's do a podcast where people
can listen to it every day."

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:37.667
It's a little bit of knowledge,
it's a little bit of wisdom,

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:38.734
and it's real quick.

00:04:38.734 --> 00:04:40.267
They're like
five-minute podcasts.

00:04:40.267 --> 00:04:41.434
-Like,
can I give a couple quotes?

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:42.634
Just see what you think of them?
-Why not?

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:44.133
I'll break them down for y'all.
-All right.

00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:45.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.934 --> 00:04:48.234
"If you're a giver,
learn your limits,

00:04:48.234 --> 00:04:50.234
because takers don't have any."

00:04:50.234 --> 00:04:51.701
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:04:51.701 --> 00:04:54.033
-Ooh. See?
Felt that game go up in you.

00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:55.434
It was like --
-Yeah.

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:56.868
Got a little game.
We got a little game here.

00:04:56.868 --> 00:04:59.100
-And, also, we call 'em --
in the hood, we call 'em jewels.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:00.167
-Oh, yeah.

00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:01.234
-Because it's something
valuable.

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:02.601
Hold on to that.
"I'mma hold on to that."

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:04.133
So, that was the jewel.
Drop another jewel right now.

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:06.367
-Yeah, here you go.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.367 --> 00:05:09.467
"Your character will outweigh
any lie told about you.

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:12.234
Those who know you, know you."

00:05:12.234 --> 00:05:14.801
[ Audience "Yeahs" ]
[ Applause ]

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:17.834
-I mean, how many times
have you heard somebody come out

00:05:17.834 --> 00:05:20.300
and try to tell a lie?
You say, "Nah, nah, nah, nah.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.667
They didn't do that.
I need more facts."

00:05:22.667 --> 00:05:25.033
You know, so --
you know, character.

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:26.367
Okay, keep going.
-Yeah, yeah, I like that.

00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:27.834
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:30.868
"I am -- I'm only responsible
for what I say,

00:05:30.868 --> 00:05:33.234
not for what you understand."

00:05:33.234 --> 00:05:35.834
[ Audience "Yeahs" ]
[ Applause ]

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:38.400
That's -- That's a jewel.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.100
-You got to --
You got to get the podcast.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:41.834
It's all over.
It's on Spotify.

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:43.534
-You know what I'm saying?
-Tune in to this.

00:05:43.534 --> 00:05:45.501
Every day, you gonna get
a little bit of something

00:05:45.501 --> 00:05:48.400
that you can -- and I'm quoting
everybody -- Aristotle --

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:51.067
I even quoted you.
-I heard this, by the way.

00:05:51.067 --> 00:05:53.100
It was today you quoted me,
and I --

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:54.901
Honestly, it meant the world
to me, you know,

00:05:54.901 --> 00:05:56.434
'cause I'm a big fan of you,
obviously.

00:05:56.434 --> 00:05:58.734
Mm-hmm.
-But I said a quote --

00:05:58.734 --> 00:06:01.968
I guess I said a quote,
"Have fun. Be silly.

00:06:01.968 --> 00:06:04.100
You're allowed to be silly.
There's nothing wrong with it."

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:06.033
-"Nothing wrong with it."
You know?

00:06:06.033 --> 00:06:07.601
And people say,
"Well, Ice, you came up,

00:06:07.601 --> 00:06:09.567
you with the gangsters."
Let me tell you, man.

00:06:09.567 --> 00:06:12.133
They tell -- They laugh,
they joke, they tell --

00:06:12.133 --> 00:06:14.434
We have more fun in the hood...
-Make fun of each other.

00:06:14.434 --> 00:06:16.567
-...just laughing,
making fun, bagging.

00:06:16.567 --> 00:06:18.868
You know, shooting the dozens
at each other.

00:06:18.868 --> 00:06:21.734
So -- And, also,
one thing about having fun,

00:06:21.734 --> 00:06:23.167
you gotta have fun.

00:06:23.167 --> 00:06:26.300
Those moments when you're really
having fun, really enjoy them.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:29.200
Don't feel guilty for them,
'cause pain is coming.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.400
Pain is guaranteed.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:32.467
That's not a joke.
Think about it.

00:06:32.467 --> 00:06:34.234
Think about it,
how often you're dealing

00:06:34.234 --> 00:06:37.234
with hardships and things,
and those few moments,

00:06:37.234 --> 00:06:40.767
when you're really happy
and laughing, enjoy them.

00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:42.801
Don't feel guilty for them
'cause they'll --

00:06:42.801 --> 00:06:44.667
Those are rare, all right?
Understand that.

00:06:44.667 --> 00:06:46.868
-Yeah, enjoy it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:46.868 --> 00:06:49.267
I love that.

00:06:49.267 --> 00:06:53.534
"Ice-T's Daily Game," IHeart and
wherever you listen to podcasts.

00:06:53.534 --> 00:06:55.467
I want to talk about
"Law &amp; Order."

00:06:55.467 --> 00:06:58.434
But I also want to bring up
your good friend,

00:06:58.434 --> 00:07:01.434
Richard Belzer,
who recently passed away.

00:07:01.434 --> 00:07:04.033
-Well --
Just what I just said, okay?

00:07:04.033 --> 00:07:06.734
So, I have one of
the greatest weeks of my life.

00:07:06.734 --> 00:07:09.901
I go out, have fun at the
Grammys, I get this star.

00:07:09.901 --> 00:07:12.434
Everybody's like, "Ice, Ice,
this is your week."

00:07:12.434 --> 00:07:15.267
Wake up the next day,
Belzer passed away.

00:07:15.267 --> 00:07:16.501
-Geez.
-See what I'm saying?

00:07:16.501 --> 00:07:17.901
-Yeah.
-So, those moments when I was

00:07:17.901 --> 00:07:20.234
having fun, that was --
that was just a short blip.

00:07:20.234 --> 00:07:22.067
And now I gotta deal with
the death

00:07:22.067 --> 00:07:24.267
of one of my
really close friends.

00:07:24.267 --> 00:07:27.267
I mean, when I came on "SVU,"
me and Belzer,

00:07:27.267 --> 00:07:29.567
we clicked really quickly.

00:07:29.567 --> 00:07:31.634
And it's like --
It's hard to talk about Belzer

00:07:31.634 --> 00:07:33.133
without being funny,
but Belzer was like --

00:07:33.133 --> 00:07:34.901
-He was one of
the funniest people on Earth.

00:07:34.901 --> 00:07:36.200
-Belzer got me real quick.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.367
He says, "Ice-T,
you're gonna be my partner.

00:07:38.367 --> 00:07:41.234
You know what I look for
in a script?"

00:07:41.234 --> 00:07:43.334
I'm like, "What?"
He goes, "Days off."

00:07:43.334 --> 00:07:46.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:46.934 --> 00:07:48.167
-That's funny.

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:50.234
-He said, "We're both
nightclub entertainers.

00:07:50.234 --> 00:07:53.767
We both don't like working late,
and we don't like working much.

00:07:53.767 --> 00:07:55.367
Me and you'll
be great partners."

00:07:55.367 --> 00:07:58.067
I said, "Well, Belzer,
you're Jewish, and I'm Black,

00:07:58.067 --> 00:08:01.334
so if -- so if the Klan come,
I just gotta outrun you."

00:08:01.334 --> 00:08:06.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:06.767 --> 00:08:08.834
-Come on, bud.

00:08:08.834 --> 00:08:10.400
Belzer, you will be missed.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:12.434
-I love Belzer, man.

00:08:12.434 --> 00:08:15.767
-Well, "Law &amp; Order: SVU"
has reached another --

00:08:15.767 --> 00:08:16.834
a new milestone.

00:08:16.834 --> 00:08:18.767
You've done over 500 episodes.

00:08:18.767 --> 00:08:22.267
It's the longest-running
drama series on TV.

00:08:22.267 --> 00:08:24.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:24.434 --> 00:08:26.567
Congratulations.

00:08:26.567 --> 00:08:28.234
Does it sink in?

00:08:28.234 --> 00:08:31.167
Do you just go, "No, this is
just -- it's just happening"?

00:08:31.167 --> 00:08:33.033
-The residuals sink in.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:33.033 --> 00:08:34.634
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-I mean --

00:08:34.634 --> 00:08:36.667
No, I mean, it's cool.
I mean, I just got on the show

00:08:36.667 --> 00:08:39.234
to do four episodes,
and it just keeps on going.

00:08:39.234 --> 00:08:42.701
And this year, we had one of the
greatest ratings seasons ever.

00:08:42.701 --> 00:08:46.000
So, we haven't been picked up
for the 25th season,

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.400
but you got Dick Wolf.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:49.434
I mean, Dick Wolf
has six shows on NBC.

00:08:49.434 --> 00:08:51.434
-Yeah, he's great.
Thank you, Dick Wolf.

00:08:51.434 --> 00:08:54.033
-We're sitting pretty,
we're sitting pretty.

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:56.968
So, we'll be back
for season 25, 26...

00:08:56.968 --> 00:08:58.834
I'mma stay on
until the wheels fall off.

00:08:58.834 --> 00:09:00.801
Black people
don't jump off boats,

00:09:00.801 --> 00:09:02.434
especially when
they're still floating.

00:09:02.434 --> 00:09:06.701
You understand?
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:06.701 --> 00:09:08.367
-That's the next
"Daily Game."

00:09:08.367 --> 00:09:11.734
-That's the next "Daily Game."
-We ain't leaving.

00:09:11.734 --> 00:09:13.467
-Can we set up this clip?
I think it'd be best

00:09:13.467 --> 00:09:15.100
to set this up
'cause it's very --

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:16.434
it's kind of interesting.

00:09:16.434 --> 00:09:18.801
-Well, in the episode, I --

00:09:18.801 --> 00:09:22.734
I spoke on my partner
to my new partner, Kevin.

00:09:22.734 --> 00:09:25.400
And I was speaking to him,
and I spoke on --

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:26.934
I didn't say Belzer's name.
-Right.

00:09:26.934 --> 00:09:29.801
-I didn't say Munch's name,
but it was a reference to him.

00:09:29.801 --> 00:09:33.501
The show came on, and three days
later, he passed away.

00:09:33.501 --> 00:09:35.801
-Here's Ice-T
in "Law &amp; Order: SVU."

00:09:35.801 --> 00:09:37.634
Take a look at this.

00:09:37.634 --> 00:09:39.434
-You're not fooling anybody.

00:09:39.434 --> 00:09:40.667
I see your armor.

00:09:40.667 --> 00:09:43.067
-Oh, humor, Fin.
-See, I had a partner,

00:09:43.067 --> 00:09:47.367
years ago,
an old homicide detective.

00:09:47.367 --> 00:09:50.334
He had the same exact
defense mechanism.

00:09:50.334 --> 00:09:52.834
-He still around?
-Ah, he retired.

00:09:52.834 --> 00:09:54.534
Guess he just ran out of gas.

00:09:54.534 --> 00:09:58.067
Last I heard,
he moved back to Baltimore.

00:09:58.067 --> 00:10:01.334
Met a divorced female rabbi.

00:10:01.334 --> 00:10:02.934
-A rabbi?
-Yeah.

00:10:02.934 --> 00:10:05.400
Yeah, and he bought back
his old cop bar.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:07.667
-[ Chuckles ]

00:10:07.667 --> 00:10:09.334
-It's about 1:30 a.m.

00:10:09.334 --> 00:10:11.868
He's probably cracking a joke
to some barfly.

00:10:11.868 --> 00:10:13.734
That skinny bastard
had a punch line

00:10:13.734 --> 00:10:15.968
for every second of the day.

00:10:15.968 --> 00:10:17.534
-Yeah.
Come on, bud.

00:10:17.534 --> 00:10:19.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
You know what I'm saying?

00:10:19.534 --> 00:10:21.701
-Yeah.
-Ice-T, everybody.

00:10:21.701 --> 00:10:24.367
"Law &amp; Order: SVU"
airs Thursdays.

00:10:24.367 --> 00:10:27.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thursdays at 9:00 p.m., on NBC.

00:10:27.567 --> 00:10:29.801
More "Tonight Show" after
the break. Stick around.

